WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.799
AI security architecture is the design of secure systems that use models, prompts, data, tools, users, integrations, and automation.

2
00:00:08.799 --> 00:00:12.427
It is not just choosing a model or writing safer prompts.

3
00:00:12.427 --> 00:00:27.092
It is the larger design discipline that decides where data flows, which identities are used, which tools are available, how actions are approved, how evidence is logged, and what happens when the system behaves unexpectedly.

4
00:00:27.092 --> 00:00:36.740
AI security overlaps with application security, data security, model risk management, and AI governance, but it is not identical to any one of them.

5
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.988
Application security protects the software and services around the AI feature.

6
00:00:41.988 --> 00:00:48.163
Data security protects sensitive information across storage, transit, retrieval, and logs.

7
00:00:48.163 --> 00:00:54.492
Model risk management addresses model behavior, evaluation, limitations, and change control.

8
00:00:54.492 --> 00:00:58.274
Governance sets policy, accountability, and oversight.

9
00:00:58.274 --> 00:01:02.056
Architecture ties those concerns into one system design.

10
00:01:02.056 --> 00:01:10.701
AI systems create new architecture questions because instructions, context, memory, retrieval, and tool use can affect outcomes.

11
00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:15.795
A traditional application usually follows code paths written by developers.

12
00:01:15.795 --> 00:01:26.601
An AI application may incorporate user instructions, system prompts, retrieved documents, model-generated tool arguments, and prior memory into a decision path.

13
00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:29.843
That does not make the model a security authority.

14
00:01:29.843 --> 00:01:35.940
It means the system needs boundaries around what the model can read, remember, decide, and do.

15
00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:49.447
Common AI application types include chat assistants, retrieval-augmented generation systems, copilots, agents, classifiers, automation workflows, and embedded AI features inside existing products.

16
00:01:49.447 --> 00:02:02.337
Each pattern has different risks, but the architectural goal is stable: make the system useful while keeping it bounded, observable, recoverable, and aligned with organizational risk decisions.

17
00:02:02.337 --> 00:02:08.126
Business value and security should reinforce each other, not compete as afterthoughts.
